Relevant columns and why we need them  
• `event_date` : restrict the analysis to 20210102  
• `event_name` : keep only the `page_view` events  
• `event_params` :  
  – key = `page_location` → full URL (needed to label PLP / PDP)  
  – key = `ga_session_id` → session id (to keep events inside the same session)  
• `user_pseudo_id` : together with `ga_session_id` uniquely defines a session  
• `event_timestamp` : ordering events inside a session, so we can see if a PDP came **after** a PLP  

Main conditions that will be reused  
1. `event_date = '20210102'`  
2. `event_name = 'page_view'`  
3. PLP label  
   – URL contains one of the category words (case–insensitive)  
   – URL does **not** contain a “+” in the last segment  
4. PDP label  
   – URL contains a “+” **and** one of the category words  
5. Session key = `user_pseudo_id || '-' || ga_session_id`  

Below are ten BigQuery queries, starting with simple inspection and finishing with the final computation.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Distinct event names that happened on 2‑Jan‑2021 (quick sanity check)
